' 2. Log writer
' The reference for this protocol. The pseudo code in 2-log-writer.md
' details each numbered step.

@startuml log-writer

skinparam style strictuml
!pragma teoz true

box "Tally proxy" #LightBlue
collections "connections" as Conns
participant "writer" as Writer
database "log" as Log
end box

note over Writer
given this run's log file and the first line, the start line, both from startup (see 1);
<latex>n</latex> the next line number, starting at 0
end note

group while the proxy runs, then on shutdown until the stop line

  Conns -> Writer : line <latex>L</latex>, through the queue

  note over Conns
    queue full: the connection
    waits; a line should never be dropped
  end note

  rnote over Writer #d1d5ef
    1. take the next line, in arrival order
  end rnote

  rnote over Writer #d1d5ef
    2. complete it
  end rnote

  rnote over Writer #ffffff
    <latex>\scriptstyle L.\mathtt{seq} \leftarrow n,\ \ L.\mathtt{client} \leftarrow \mathtt{client},\ \ L.\mathtt{time} \leftarrow \mathtt{now}</latex>
  end rnote

  rnote over Writer #d1d5ef
    3. append it and force it to disk
  end rnote

  Writer -> Log : append <latex>L</latex>, force to disk

  alt if it worked

    Writer --> Conns : on disk

    rnote over Writer #ffffff
      <latex>\scriptstyle n \leftarrow n + 1</latex>
    end rnote

    opt if <latex>L.\mathtt{event} = \mathtt{stop}</latex>

      Writer --> Conns : error, to every line after it

    end

  else

    rnote over Writer #d1d5ef
      4. print the error, stop the proxy (see 1)
    end rnote

    Writer --> Conns : error, to this connection and every waiting one

  end

end

@enduml
